# Phase 11: threads in one process: a mutex keeps a counter exact, each
# thread has its own thread-local variables and errno, the allocator works
# from every thread at once, and exit or a fault ends every thread.
cerberus kernel shell
!send run /bin/threadtest
!wait 30
8 threads added 100000 each under a mutex: exactly 800000
every thread kept its own thread-local variables and errno
8 threads allocated and freed at once without stepping on each other
two threads took 1000 turns through a condition variable
exit and a fault each ended every thread of their process
threadtest: PASS
run: /bin/threadtest exited with status 0
